WEBVTT

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.780
India got 5 degrees hotter.

00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:04.610
But imagine if the entire
country became 5 degrees colder!

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:07.300
Cities like Delhi could
experience much harsher winters.

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:11.350
Places that already receive snowfall
could face even more extreme cold.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:13.460
But the biggest impact
wouldn't just be on people.

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:15.090
Agriculture could change dramatically.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.630
Some crops might benefit
from cooler conditions,

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:20.870
while others could face frost
damage or disrupted growing seasons.

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:22.960
Energy demand for heating would rise,

00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:25.500
transport could be
disrupted in colder regions,

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:27.520
and ecosystems would have to adapt.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.010
Five degrees sounds small.

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:31.380
But across an entire country,
it's enormous.

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:32.230
Tomorrow,

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:36.130
what happens if one of India's most
important natural barriers disappears?

